{#
  Who wrote something, linked to their archive when the site knows them.

  `author` is what the CMS puts on the context for a document's `author` front
  matter (TASK-67): an object with `name` to print and, for a name that is one
  of this site's users, `username`, `url` and whatever profile they have
  written. A name nobody here answers to has the `name` and nothing else, so it
  is printed without a link rather than left off — the file said somebody wrote
  this, and that is worth saying even when they have no account.

  Import it with `{% import "partials/byline.njk" as byline %}`; the argument
  carries everything, so it needs no context.
#}
{% macro line(author) %}
{%- if author %}
      <span class="p-author h-card">
        {%- if author.url %}
        <a class="u-url" href="{{ author.url | url }}">{{ author.name }}</a>
        {%- else %}
        {{ author.name }}
        {%- endif %}
      </span>
{%- endif %}
{%- endmacro %}
